@startuml
title F06 - Explicit I'm OK check-in
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
actor "Resident" as Resident
control "H06\nHub resident interface" as H06
control "H02\nHub persistence" as H02
control "H05\nHub rules adapter" as H05
control "S02\nDeterministic rules core" as S02
control "H08\nHub cloud link" as H08
control "B07\nRead models/API" as B07
boundary "A02\nApp home" as A02
Resident -> H06: Press the dedicated I'm OK button
H06 -> H02: Create and durably commit explicit check-in event
H02 --> H06: Return saved-local feedback immediately
H02 -> H05: Apply check-in to current routine window
H05 -> S02: Record explicit evidence and stable event ID
H02 -> H08: Queue cloud replay without changing occurrence time
H08 -> B07: Update household timeline/read model
A02 -> B07: Fetch explicit check-in and freshness
B07 --> A02: Return evidence; no automatic safe/well label
note over Resident,A02: Outcome - The resident receives honest local feedback and the caregiver sees an explicit check-in separately from inferred activity.
@enduml
